From 1b68f41e538b8cb6517098a10b4afd4fd8a3d753 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:24:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): review of #3912: deltas equal a fresh page,
 quieter early passes [daveey]

- Route: a direct call keeps Query() defaults; only an int after_id takes the
  delta path (the red tests/hermes_cli/test_history_commentary_display.py shard).
- state.db: a new messages_visibility_revision_update trigger bumps
  transcript_revision when a row's active/compacted flag changes (queued-prompt
  drain, model-switch pivot, rewind, compaction), so a cached tail extended by
  deltas refetches instead of keeping a row a fresh page hides.
- Delta read: one snapshot (transcript_read_snapshot) for revision, anchor and
  rows; the revision sums the resume lineage (ancestor rewrites count); a new row
  the latest page would fold (same display identity, later archived-tool copy)
  reports fold_conflict and the Desktop refetches the page.
- Delta responses over 16 KiB use the latest page's gzip path.
- change_watcher: a failed cursor or row read keeps the old cursor for that store
  (retried next pass, no floor started); sessions the listings never show
  (hidden, tool, subagent, delegate children) are not pushed.
- Prefetcher: an untracked mover asks for an early listing pass only when its
  (connection, profile) is listed, and one a forced pass did not pick up is
  ignored for 10 min; a gateway without the after_id route is probed again after
  10 min.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
